<title>TURKMENISTAN: Turkmen parliament examines 97 budget draft Dec 20.</title>
<headline>Turkmen parliament examines 97 budget draft Dec 20.</headline>
<dateline>ASHGABAT 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkmenistan's parliament will consider the 1997 draft budget on December 20, President Saparmurat Niyazov said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He said the draft envisaged income of 4.99 trillion manat and expenditure of 5.06 trillion. &quot;The growth in the volume of the budget will come about by doubling sales of natural gas,&quot; Niyazov said.</p>
<p>Niyazov said Turkmenistan would export 40 billion cubic metres of gas in 1997, up from 24 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>($=4,055 manat)</p>
</text>
